PART 30 - YOUTUBE ARCHITECTURE EXPLANATION
====================================================================

SAY:

"In this project, we are starting with a basic AWS EC2 instance
running Ubuntu Linux.

The first layer is the infrastructure layer, where AWS EC2
provides our Linux server.

We connect to the server using SSH.

Inside the server, we perform Linux administration such as
user management, permissions, process management and disk
management.

For the application layer, we install Nginx and deploy a
simple website.

We use systemd to manage the Nginx service and Nginx logs
to troubleshoot application requests and errors.

Then we introduce automation using Bash.

Our first script performs a server health check by checking
CPU load, memory, disk usage, processes and Nginx status.

Our second script creates backups of Nginx logs.

Finally, Cron automatically executes our backup script on
a schedule.

The complete project is maintained using Git and GitHub.

So this project demonstrates the complete flow from server
provisioning, Linux administration, application deployment,
monitoring, automation and version control."


